---
# Clang-tidy configuration for the host test/runner harness.
#
# The check set mirrors the root .clang-tidy (this nearest config fully
# replaces it for files under host/); the only difference is the cognitive
# complexity threshold. Test functions are long sequential lists of verify
# blocks, which inflate cognitive complexity without indicating the nested
# decision logic the check exists to catch. The threshold is therefore a
# ratchet set above the current worst function (84) and should be lowered
# over time as tests are decomposed (see docs/quality.md, issue #76).
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*,
  misc-*,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -misc-non-private-member-variables-in-classes,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
CheckOptions:
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: '100'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.DescribeBasicIncrements: 'true'
